@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
' purpose: why the e2e suite drives a real terminal, and why the pane is not the evidence
' covers: internal/tmux/tmux.go
'
' ── THE AGENTS ONLY EXIST AT A TTY ─────────────────────────────────────────
' Every harness proveo runs is an interactive terminal program. Pipe its stdout
' and it behaves differently or not at all, so an e2e suite that captured output
' the ordinary way would be testing a mode no operator ever uses. tmux gives the
' tests a real terminal to drive, which is the only way the interactive paths —
' the choice form, the login prompt, ptyproxy — are reachable from a test at all.
'
' ── THE PANE IS NOT THE RECORD ─────────────────────────────────────────────
' Learned the hard way, and it is the reason assertions read a TRANSCRIPT rather
' than the pane: a one-shot agent prints its last message and exits inside a
' single poll interval, and once the session is gone CaptureAll can only return
' what was captured before it died. The model's final answer was being lost even
' on runs where the model had said it. Tests therefore tee the whole run to a file
' and assert against that; the pane is only used to notice that the session ended.
' Line wrapping is the second reason — a pane wraps, a transcript does not.
'
' ── INJECTABLE RUNNER ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' Runner is a one-method interface declared here because here is where it is
' consumed, and the package's own tests use a recorder that scripts stdout per
' call. So the argv construction and the wait-for-text loop are unit-testable
' without tmux installed, while Available() keeps the e2e suite honest about
' skipping on a host that lacks it.
title internal/tmux — a real terminal, and a transcript rather than a pane

participant "e2e test" as T <<app>>
participant "tmux.Session" as S <<app>>
participant "pane" as P <<error>>
participant "transcript file" as F <<data>>

T ARROW_MAIN S : Start(w, h, sh -c "... | tee run.log")
S ARROW_QUEUE P : CaptureAll — only to notice the session ended
S ARROW_MAIN F : every byte, unwrapped
F ARROW_MAIN T : assertions read HERE

note over P
  **The pane loses the ending.** A one-shot agent
  prints its last message and exits within one
  poll; after that CaptureAll returns only what it
  already had. The reply was lost even when the
  model had given it.
end note
@enduml
